WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.100
- [Narrator] The race to be
the next speaker of the House

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.170
is down to these two.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.020
Jim Jordan is known for
being a fiery attack dog

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:07.860
in his committees.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.270
- I don't want you to answer my question.

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:12.000
The American people want Dr.
Fauci to answer the question.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.490
- [Narrator] And being a
frequent voice on "Fox News."

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:17.460
- The left is, you know, their
religion is climate change.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.330
- [Narrator] Steve Scalise,

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.310
while he spends less
time in the spotlight,

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.590
became a national figure after being shot

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:26.040
practicing for the congressional
baseball game in 2017.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.380
- Both Republican and
Democrat reached out.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.680
It really does show the
warm side of Congress

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.690
that very few people get to see.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.370
- [Narrator] And is popular in his party

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.930
for his career and leadership,

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.150
building consensus among members.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:42.030
Here's how these two charted
a course to the speakers race,

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.340
and how they represent two different paths

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.070
for the future of House Republicans.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.610
Jordan actually got his first
vote for speaker back in 2013.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.410
- [Reading Clerk] Jordan of Ohio.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.910
- [Narrator] It was more of a protest vote

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:55.740
against then Speaker John Boehner

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.320
as were the two votes he
got again two years later.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.940
- Jordan. Jordan.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.290
- [Narrator] That year,
the majority leader

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.320
lost his election and Kevin
McCarthy moved up from whip

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.150
to the number two position,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.910
and a new face joined
the leadership, Scalise.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:10.740
- We're gonna continue to
move forward in the House

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.270
as a united team.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.370
- [Narrator] At the same
time, Jordan co-founded

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:17.040
the anti-establishment
House Freedom Caucus,

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.470
made up of more conservative
members of the House

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.060
angry Republican priorities

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.220
were not making it into negotiations

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.530
with the Democratic
White House and Senate.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.530
They ultimately pushed
Boehner to resign that fall.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:29.790
- Well, are they unrealistic

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.590
about what can be done in government?

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:32.640
That's the dysfunction.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.890
- Absolutely, they're unrealistic.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:35.723
- [Narrator] Jordan's caucus

00:01:35.723 --> 00:01:37.890
also blocked McCarthy from moving up,

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.583
electing Paul Ryan after
forcing McCarthy to drop out.

00:01:40.583 --> 00:01:42.900
- I think I shocked some of you, huh.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:44.670
- [Narrator] And Jordan
later challenged McCarthy

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.020
for the role of leader.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.430
He lost.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:49.350
So when the speakership opened up again,

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:53.177
McCarthy moved up, but not
without some protest votes.

00:01:53.177 --> 00:01:54.677
- Jim Jordan.

00:01:54.677 --> 00:01:55.950
- [Reading Clerk] Jordan.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.170
- [Narrator] And Scalise
moved up to leader.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.280
- As the majority leader,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:02.340
I really look forward to
bringing those bills to the floor

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.620
through a committee
process that's open again.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.520
- [Narrator] But while their paths

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.320
to the speaker battle have differed,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.900
their backgrounds are remarkably similar.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.760
They both represent their hometowns

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.740
and win reelection easily.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.440
They both started their political
careers at the same time

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.060
and around the same age

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.940
as state representatives
and eventually senators

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.690
before becoming Congressmen
also around the same time.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:26.790
Politically, they're
both very conservative

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.470
and both supported Trump's efforts

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.390
to overturn the 2020 election.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.100
- Do you think the election was stolen?

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.180
- And it's not just irregular.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.760
It's states that did
not follow the laws set

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.190
which the Constitution says
they're supposed to follow.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:41.190
- 80 million Americans, 80
million of our fellow citizens,

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:44.130
Republicans and Democrats, have
doubts about this election.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.930
- [Narrator] Although
Jordan is much closer

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.160
to Trump personally.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.370
- There's so many weak Republicans,
and we have great ones.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.260
Jim Jordan and some of these guys,

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.990
they're out there fighting,
the House guys are fighting.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.640
- [Narrator] January 6th wasn't Jordan's

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.590
first brush with controversy.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.800
In 2018, former Ohio
State University students

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.320
from Jordan's time as an
assistant wrestling coach

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.260
claimed he knew about sexual
abuse by the team doctor,

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.780
but Jordan has denied this.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.280
While they have a lot in common,

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.230
the primary difference between the two

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:15.060
is in their beliefs of how to utilize

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.180
their slim Republican
majority in Congress.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.160
Scalise is pitching himself as the one

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.680
with the experience and
personal relationships

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.800
from his time in leadership to
bring party members together.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.150
- I've got a long proven record

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.250
as somebody who knows
how to unify Republicans

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.780
to fight on the battles that matter

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.670
for the families who
gave us this majority.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:33.930
- [Narrator] Although
he's currently battling

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.300
a blood cancer he says is very treatable.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.640
- If the doctors didn't sign
off, I wouldn't be doing this.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.620
- [Narrator] Jordan,
however, is pitching himself

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.970
as the person who could unite

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:43.890
the more far right members of the party

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.960
who are frustrated Republican priorities

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:48.300
are again left out of negotiations.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.770
- I do think we have to have someone

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.330
who can bring our team together.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.980
I think I'm best equipped to do that.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.290
- [Narrator] So House
Republicans will have to decide.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.000
Do they finally give the rebel a try

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.476
or stick with the established successor?

00:03:59.476 --> 00:04:02.059
(gentle music)

